# =============================================================================
# AII Smart Paper Maker — environment variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
# (`.gitignore` already ignores `.env` and `.env.*`.)
#
# python-dotenv loads `.env` automatically at startup, so you do NOT need to
# export these variables into your shell manually.
#
# That sentence was NOT true until 2026-08-20, and the gap was silent. `.env` was
# loaded inside app/services/ai_service.py, which is late: DB_PATH and
# PAPER_MAKER_API_KEY are read when their own modules are imported, and those ran
# first. So a DB_PATH set here was dropped and the app quietly built a new, empty
# database in the project root; a PAPER_MAKER_API_KEY set here was dropped and the
# API came up with no auth at all. Both measured, both fixed by loading `.env` in
# app/__init__.py, which runs before any `app.*` module. See PROGRESS.md 2026-08-20.
#
# PRECEDENCE, measured: a real environment variable BEATS this file, which beats
# the code default. python-dotenv does not overwrite variables that are already
# set, so `set DB_PATH=...` or NSSM's AppEnvironmentExtra still wins.
#
# `.env` is found by walking UP from the current working directory. The launchers
# do `cd /d "%~dp0"` first, so they always find this project's file -- but running
# uvicorn by hand from some other folder can pick up a different `.env`, or none.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI provider keys — set AT LEAST ONE of the two below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider priority is fixed in code: if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, Claude is
# used and GEMINI_API_KEY is ignored. Otherwise Gemini is used. If neither is
# set, question/syllabus generation fails at request time (the rest of the app
# still runs).

# Google Gemini — FREE, no credit card required. Recommended for testing.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com  ("Get API key").
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# Anthropic Claude — paid, higher quality. Recommended for production.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com
# If this is set, it wins over GEMINI_API_KEY automatically.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-anthropic-api-key-here


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access control — DO RAASTE, aur behtar wala DB mein hai, is file mein nahi
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SEC-02 (2026-09-12) ke baad app ke paas ASLI USERS hain: har teacher ka apna
# account, password, role (admin/teacher), server-side session, aur har login ka
# log. Wo kisi env var se on nahi hota — pehla user banate hi khud ba khud chalu
# ho jata hai:
#
#     python scripts/create_admin.py        (server par, ek dafa)
#
# Us ke baad /api sirf login se khulta hai aur neeche wali shared key /api ke
# liye kaam karna chhor deti hai. Teachers ka rasta: http://<server>:8000/login.html
#
# Jab tak koi user nahi bana, app bilkul pehle jaisi chalti hai — yani ye
# upgrade kisi chalti hui school ko subah bahar nahi karta. Neeche wali key usi
# soorat ke liye hai.
#
# KYA FARQ HAI. Shared key sirf darwaza band karti hai; wo ye nahi janti ke
# andar kaun aaya. Users mode janta hai: kis ne parcha banaya, kis ne mitaya,
# kaun kab andar aaya, aur kis naam par nakaam koshishein ho rahi hain.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access control — API key (users na bane hon to STRONGLY recommended)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set ho to har /api endpoint is key ko `x-api-key` header mein maangega (warna
# 401). Frontend user se key ek dafa maangta hai aur localStorage mein rakh leta
# hai. UNSET chhodo to auth OFF rehta hai (local dev) — par production mein
# ISE ZAROOR SET KARO, warna koi bhi tumhare AI tokens (paisa) aur DB use kar
# sakta hai. Koi bhi lambi random string chalti hai.
#
# FAIL-CLOSED: agar app kisi deployment par chal raha ho (Railway ke inject kiye
# hue env markers, ya PAPER_MAKER_REQUIRE_API_KEY=1) aur ye key set na ho, to app
# start hi nahi hogi (silently unprotected chalne ki bajaye loud crash). Local
# dev is se bacha rehta hai.
# ── DB_PATH — SCHOOL SETUP KI SAB SE AHEM LINE ────────────────────────────────
# Ye line yahan 2026-09-08 (UI-106) mein aayi. Pehle is file mein DB_PATH ka zikr
# SIRF comments mein tha, koi set karne wali line nahi -- aur `docs/SETUP-LOCAL.md`
# step 5 kehta hai "`.env.example` ki copy banao" aur teen lines dikhata hai jin
# mein pehli DB_PATH hai. Yani jo bhi guide par chalta, us ki `.env` mein wahi
# ek var GHAYAB hota jise guide khud "sab se ahem line" kehta hai.
#
# ⚠ GHALAT YA TYPO'D PATH PAR APP ERROR NAHI DETI -- wo us jagah nayi KHALI
# database bana leti hai, folder samet, aur school ko lagta hai saara data urh
# gaya jab ke asli file apni jagah salamat hoti hai. Naapa gaya 2026-09-08:
# DB_PATH=C:/PaperMaker/nowhere/typo.db chup-chaap resolve ho jata hai.
# `start-school.bat` chalne se PEHLE check karta hai ke file waqai mojood hai.
#
# Set na karo to DB repo folder ke andar banti hai (dev ke liye theek, school ke
# liye nahi -- git operations us ke saath cheer-chaar kar sakti hain).
# DB_PATH=C:\PaperMakerData\paper_maker.db

# PAPER_MAKER_API_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Kisi bhi host par (jahan Railway markers na hon) auth ko mandatory banana ho to
# ise 1 kar do — phir key missing hone par app fail-closed ho jayegi.
# PAPER_MAKER_REQUIRE_API_KEY=1

# CORS: comma-separated origins jo browser se /api call kar sakti hain. Frontend
# same-origin (`/`) se serve hota hai to ise set karne ki zaroorat aam taur par
# nahi. UNSET = koi cross-origin allowed nahi (sirf same-origin) — yeh safe
# default hai. Sirf tab set karo jab API ko kisi doosri domain se call karna ho.
# PAPER_MAKER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://paper.myschool.edu.pk


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database location (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute or relative path to the SQLite file. Defaults to `paper_maker.db`
# in the project root. On an ephemeral host point this at a mounted persistent
# volume so data survives redeploys.
#
# ON THE SCHOOL SERVER THIS IS THE ONE SETTING WORTH DOUBLE-CHECKING. A wrong or
# mistyped path does NOT raise an error -- the app creates a new empty database at
# it, parent folder and all, and every existing paper appears to be gone while the
# real file sits untouched wherever it actually lives. `start-school.bat` checks
# that the resolved file exists and asks before starting if it does not; that
# prompt is the last thing standing between a typo here and a panicked morning.
#
# Windows (school): DB_PATH=C:\PaperMakerData\paper_maker.db
# Container/volume: DB_PATH=/data/paper_maker.db
# DB_PATH=/data/paper_maker.db


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PDF export — LibreOffice binary (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for PDF export, and only if LibreOffice is installed somewhere
# non-standard. The app auto-detects the binary via: SOFFICE_PATH -> system
# PATH -> common install locations. Word (.docx) export needs no LibreOffice.
# SOFFICE_PATH=C:\Program Files\LibreOffice\program\soffice.exe


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server port (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not read by the app directly — used by the deploy start command
# (`uvicorn ... --port $PORT`). Railway injects this automatically. For local
# development pass `--port 8000` on the uvicorn command line instead.
# PORT=8000
